# Intent: Owner's hands-on test, part 2. The quick settings screen (the stock panel the sheet's More tile opens) and the More screens (time zone, network test, version, games) could not be dismissed: their column of controls ran off the 240 px glass and pushed Done out of sight. Both are rebuilt with fixed positions: a grabber handle at the top, a Done or Back target 108 by 44 at the top right, 44 px controls with the 20 px font, two Wi-Fi rows folded into one row of up to three networks, and a swipe down (or a tap on the empty background of quick settings) closes them. The More menu is a two by two grid; a sub page's swipe down goes back to the menu.
# Placement: unit
# Upstream: firmware/main/hal/board/stackchan_display.cc (stock quick panel, patched R01, U03) and maipai_more.cc (ours, U03 to U05)
# Check after a flash: Open the sheet, tap More: quick settings shows Done at the top right, a handle, big sliders; swipe down closes it; More opens a grid and Back or a swipe down returns.

